					"uidString" : "1qczBgHAQHeMNa1UtYBq0w=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "The bridge uses an event-driven architecture: when a BEAM module recompiles, one announcement fans out to all GT surfaces displaying derived state for that module — Functions tab, Source tab, |> expander coders, browser sidebar, etc. The announcement carries the new function-entry list inline, so subscribers re-render directly from the payload without a follow-up bridge call.\n\nThis page walks through the architecture component by component. Each section is followed by an example or live view you can run."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-27T00:36:32.501741+08:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-27T00:36:32.501741+08:00"
