				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Per-module routing\n\nA subscriber that only cares about one module registers with `BeamEventAnnouncer for: aModuleName` — narrow events only. Events for other modules never wake it up. Subscribers that want every recompile (e.g. {{gtClass:name=ElixirCoderBrowser}}) listen on `BeamEventAnnouncer default`.\n\nThe dispatcher fans every recompile event out to both channels: the per-module announcer (if any subscribers exist for that module) AND the default singleton. See {{gtMethod:name=BeamEventAnnouncer class>>announceRecompiledFrom:}}."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-27T00:36:40.918469+08:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-27T00:36:40.918469+08:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "qcGThVwqQ8+iJzfDElKLNw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Payload-carrying broadcasts\n\nA {{gtClass:name=BeamModuleRecompiled}} announcement carries the new function-entry list inline (when the BEAM produced it for the directly-saved module). Subscribers re-render from the payload directly — no follow-up `Analysis.all_functions/1` round-trip per surface.\n\nThe example below proves it: subscribe a tap, save HotReloadTest, and the announcement arrives with `functions` populated."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "pharoSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-27T00:36:42.172282+08:00"
					}
