					"uidString" : "HhsaKbmmRhiNMzxwo39z5A=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## Lifecycle: weak subscriptions\n\nEvery subscriber registration uses `weak when:send:to:` so closed inspectors and GC'd coders don't pin themselves alive in the registry. The Fanout view above is the easiest way to see this in action — close a coder, force a GC, refresh the view: the receiver disappears.\n\nBloc elements with non-trivial event-handler work (e.g. {{gtClass:name=ElixirCoderBrowser}}'s sidebar fan-out) subscribe in `onAddedToSceneGraph` and unsubscribe in `onRemovedFromSceneGraph` so background instances stay silent. The browser's own handler does pure invalidation — drops `rawNodes` so the next user interaction refetches lazily — which keeps a save-fan-out from triggering 50+ round trips per browser."
			},
			{
				"__type" : "textSnippet",
				"children" : {
					"__type" : "snippets",
					"items" : [ ]
				},
				"createEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"createTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-27T00:37:01.329067+08:00"
					}
				},
				"editEmail" : {
					"__type" : "email",
					"emailString" : "<unknown>"
				},
				"editTime" : {
					"__type" : "time",
					"time" : {
						"__type" : "dateAndTime",
						"dateAndTimeString" : "2026-04-27T00:37:01.329067+08:00"
					}
				},
				"uid" : {
					"__type" : "uid",
					"uidString" : "tIp18ys5Tu2trXg9WXpkHw=="
				},
				"paragraphStyle" : {
					"__type" : "textStyle"
				},
				"string" : "## BEAM-side mirror\n\nOn the BEAM side the same pattern lives in {{gtClass:name=GtBridge.Events}} via the EventBroker library — `%ModuleEvent{kind: :recompiled, mod: ..., source_hash: ...}` events fan out to subscribers like `GtBridge.CacheReaper` (invalidates the per-module ETS cache) and `GtBridge.Xref` (replaces the module's call-graph entries). The HTTP response carries the same `recompiled` payload list to GT, where {{gtMethod:name=ElixirModuleCoder>>announceBeamRecompiledFrom:}} fans out to {{gtClass:name=BeamEventAnnouncer}}.\n\nLive regression coverage: {{gtClass:name=BeamEventBusExamples}} has 17 examples covering the announcer dispatch, the per-module routing, payload propagation, cross-coder sync, source/functions tab refresh, and the browser invalidation path. Each example is runnable from the inspector."
			}
		]
	},
